WEBVTT

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:26.690
A tragedy must have occurred.

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:30.730
That's the only reason I'd be here.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:34.360
I'm going to be sick of
your face soon enough.

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:39.080
Were you killed by
the Mountain Dogs? By Takano?

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:45.460
I couldn't tell you. I can't remember
the hours leading up to my death.

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:47.250
But I don't think I was.

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:52.460
I remember running out of that classroom
hellbent on killing myself.

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:56.800
I can't remember if I found a knife
to slit my throat or drowned myself.

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:00.220
What happened on that fragment?

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:03.680
I'm sorry, I know you don't
want to think about it...

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:06.270
Insubstantial as I am,

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:11.150
I cannot view your fragments,
let alone join you in them.

00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:16.990
Still, discussing what happened
might help us understand this situation.

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:23.000
I think Keiichi and Rena
killed each other...

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:26.500
...as a result of paranoia
caused by Hinamizawa Syndrome.

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:29.500
That's horrible.

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:31.420
For Keiichi, for Rena,

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:33.880
and for your heart, Rika.

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:34.880
Agreed.

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:37.050
I knew Keiichi was suspicious
and fearful of Rena's behavior,

00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:41.050
but I'd thought my words to him had
convinced him everything was all right.

00:01:41.050 --> 00:01:43.390
How wrong I was to believe that.

00:01:43.390 --> 00:01:46.270
You shouldn't blame yourself.

00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:49.310
Even if your centuries
of scars are fading,

00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:53.730
they will never disappear.

00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:56.150
Believe me, I'm well aware.

00:01:56.150 --> 00:01:59.070
People cannot live on without hope.

00:01:59.070 --> 00:02:01.950
That's why I refuse to give in to despair.

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:05.830
It's only one failure.

00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:08.000
Hanyuu...

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:10.460
I shouldn't have been mean to you earlier.

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:15.760
Talking with you now has made
my heart feel a little bit lighter.

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:21.640
I'm sorry for saying
I would be sick of your face.

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:27.140
Rika, I know you'll make it out of this.

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:31.060
Just like before,
you <i>will </i>create a miracle.

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:32.560
Right.

00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:44.700
Breaking her spirit
will not be easy, it seems.

00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:50.750
Goodness, my neck still hurts.

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:53.130
Even though I know
it's no more than a memory,

00:02:53.130 --> 00:02:59.880
I still feel the knife slicing into
my neck. It's quite unpleasant, Eua-san.

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:05.930
That is because my power is
at full strength, unlike that failure.

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:10.560
Though if you'd prefer,
I can also grant you memory loss,

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:13.690
much like the ability
that failure gifted the cat.

00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:16.980
I was merely grousing, that's all.

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:23.740
You've already given me a special ability,
Eua-san. It's more than enough.

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:26.580
If you die after the cat,

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:31.080
then you will travel with her
to the same fragment.

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:34.170
That's right, and I won't
let her out of my sight.

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:39.420
Besides, knowing Rika,
she likely believes Takano is behind this.

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:41.380
Because in your previous fragment,

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:48.350
Keiichi seemed to succumb to the syndrome,
much like he did in the past.

00:03:48.350 --> 00:03:50.430
I'm terribly sorry, Rika,

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:54.400
but your hundred years
of experience will not help you

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:57.230
when you're living in worlds
where I control the curse!

00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:03.490
You are so very amusing.

00:04:03.490 --> 00:04:08.580
Now, how will you entertain me next?

00:05:37.330 --> 00:05:41.000
"Higurashi: When They Cry SOTSU"

00:05:50.470 --> 00:05:52.970
"Sunday, June 5th"

00:05:57.020 --> 00:05:58.730
Good morning.

00:05:58.730 --> 00:06:00.980
Good morning, Rika!

00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:04.360
My, you look a bit pale.

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:08.990
I woke up from a scary dream.

00:06:08.990 --> 00:06:13.200
I'm sorry to hear that.
What happened in the dream?

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:15.540
I've already forgotten all about it.

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:18.870
Besides, it was just a dream!

00:06:29.260 --> 00:06:34.260
Rika, you know full well
that was no dream.

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:40.150
I'll admit, you know how
to use a blade quite well.

00:06:40.150 --> 00:06:45.110
But I'd like to find a method that's
a bit more pleasant next time.

00:07:06.840 --> 00:07:09.680
Stop pesterin' me, asshole!

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:11.050
S-Satoko!

00:07:11.050 --> 00:07:12.800
Hello, Uncle.

00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:18.390
I-I'm sorry! I thought you were that
asshole landlady here to complain again!

00:07:18.390 --> 00:07:19.730
I'm so sorry for yelling at you!

00:07:19.730 --> 00:07:23.440
If I'd known it was you,
I would've opened the door with a smile!

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:26.190
One just like this!

00:07:26.190 --> 00:07:29.900
Very well. I forgive you.

00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:32.160
Y-You mean it?

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:36.830
I can't keep ya standing out here!
Come inside and have some tea!

00:07:36.830 --> 00:07:38.910
A-Actually, let's go to
the mahjong parlor--

00:07:38.910 --> 00:07:41.710
Er, or a café to get something sweet!

00:07:41.710 --> 00:07:44.840
Thank you for offering,
but I'd rather not.

00:07:44.840 --> 00:07:46.920
O-Oh, sorry.

00:07:46.920 --> 00:07:52.510
I just don't know what kind of stuff
a girl your age might prefer.

00:07:52.510 --> 00:07:56.140
You can make it up to me
by doing me a favor.

00:07:56.140 --> 00:08:01.350
Of course! Whatever I can do for ya,
I'll happily help out with!

00:08:01.350 --> 00:08:07.570
There's a special place I'd like to go,
but they won't let me in by myself.

00:08:12.070 --> 00:08:15.570
That's it! Keep the pressure on 'im!

00:08:15.570 --> 00:08:19.080
One horse is racing ahead of the pack--
by God, it's Wanyan Daio!

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:24.750
Wait, look who's coming out wide!
It's Cheshire Cat Munchy!

00:08:24.750 --> 00:08:27.380
Wanyan Daio's in the lead!
But will it be Cheshire Cat Munchy?!

00:08:27.380 --> 00:08:29.210
Go! Go!

00:08:30.550 --> 00:08:34.930
"Race 6 Winner"

00:08:30.550 --> 00:08:34.930
And it's Wanyan Daio with the win,
and Cheshire Cat Munchy with second!

00:08:34.930 --> 00:08:36.300
"Race bet: Top two finishers"

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:40.600
Yes! We won!

00:08:41.100 --> 00:08:46.230
1 in 380 odds! Three hundred and eighty!

00:08:46.230 --> 00:08:48.190
Satoko!

00:08:48.190 --> 00:08:50.570
You were right on the money!

00:08:50.570 --> 00:08:52.900
You're the goddess of good luck!

00:08:52.900 --> 00:08:54.950
Uncle!

00:08:54.950 --> 00:08:57.160
S-Sorry, I was excited...

00:08:57.160 --> 00:08:58.950
Let's go home.

00:08:58.950 --> 00:09:03.000
My magic only works once.

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:04.830
S-Satoko...

00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:21.060
I cannot believe it.

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:26.100
How can men live like this
with no qualms whatsoever?

00:09:26.100 --> 00:09:27.730
It's embarrassing.

00:09:27.730 --> 00:09:32.990
Uncle, please gather up all the trash in
this room. There's nowhere for us to sit.

00:09:32.990 --> 00:09:36.070
And you should put your futon
away every morning!

00:09:36.070 --> 00:09:38.030
There's nothin' wrong
with leavin' it out--

00:09:38.030 --> 00:09:39.620
What was that?

00:09:39.620 --> 00:09:41.330
Y-Yes, ma'am.

00:09:55.420 --> 00:09:56.840
So, Satoko...

00:09:56.840 --> 00:09:59.340
I was thinking about it,

00:09:59.340 --> 00:10:03.930
and I think you should have half
this cash--no, more than half, please.

00:10:05.270 --> 00:10:08.560
This is more than enough for me.

00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:11.060
The rest is all yours, Uncle.

00:10:11.060 --> 00:10:13.360
N-No, I couldn't!

00:10:13.360 --> 00:10:16.360
You paid for the bet.

00:10:16.360 --> 00:10:21.410
All I did was tell you the name
of the horse I dreamed about.

00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:25.290
Th-Thank you, Satoko! I owe ya!

00:10:25.290 --> 00:10:27.620
Don't be so glum, Uncle.

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:33.050
This was quite the windfall.
We've got to celebrate.

00:10:33.050 --> 00:10:36.630
Thanks, but my doctor says I shouldn't.

00:10:36.630 --> 00:10:41.720
One measly drink couldn't hurt.
Besides, we're celebrating.

00:10:41.720 --> 00:10:45.640
I guess you're right. Just one is fine.

00:10:45.640 --> 00:10:48.350
I'll enjoy this soda.

00:10:52.690 --> 00:10:56.400
I'm so goddamn happy.

00:10:56.400 --> 00:11:01.030
My cute niece is bein' so damn nice.

00:11:01.030 --> 00:11:06.330
She's so nice,
but I was such an asshole...

00:11:06.330 --> 00:11:09.670
I'm so sorry, Satoko! Please forgive me!

00:11:09.670 --> 00:11:12.920
It's all in the past.
You're all right, Uncle.

00:11:12.920 --> 00:11:18.380
I'm not all right!
I've gotta keep you safe, Satoko!

00:11:18.380 --> 00:11:20.430
How very dependable of you.

00:11:20.430 --> 00:11:23.800
Though I still can't help but worry.

00:11:23.800 --> 00:11:29.890
You have some scary friends,
don't you, Uncle? I don't like scary men.

00:11:29.890 --> 00:11:34.770
Y-Yeah, I hung out with
a scary crowd in the past.

00:11:34.770 --> 00:11:37.360
But don't worry,
I ain't associated with them anymore.

00:11:37.360 --> 00:11:40.150
So you don't have any way
of contacting them?

00:11:40.150 --> 00:11:42.780
I do, in my address book.

00:11:42.780 --> 00:11:45.660
That's so scary.

00:11:45.660 --> 00:11:49.910
What if someone finds your address book
and you get in trouble?

00:11:52.330 --> 00:11:54.460
Don't worry 'bout it.

00:11:54.460 --> 00:12:01.380
Even if the cops peeked through it,
I put everyone under fake names.

00:12:02.800 --> 00:12:05.510
You're so smart, Uncle.

00:12:10.390 --> 00:12:17.820
Let's say I wanted to buy something
<i>dangerous </i>that I couldn't buy elsewhere.

00:12:17.820 --> 00:12:20.820
Which one of those
fake names would sell that?

00:12:28.790 --> 00:12:30.290
"Kawauchi"

00:12:33.540 --> 00:12:36.040
"Flower Road"

00:13:08.160 --> 00:13:11.790
This ain't your daddy's car, sweetie.

00:13:11.790 --> 00:13:15.290
My, I thought I used
the correct number of knocks.

00:13:15.290 --> 00:13:18.170
That is why you opened the door, yes?

00:13:18.170 --> 00:13:21.000
I got no beef with you, sweetie.

00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:24.010
You should get the hell away from
whoever you're workin' for.

00:13:24.010 --> 00:13:26.050
I brought cash.

00:13:26.050 --> 00:13:31.310
Look, deals like this only happen
if we trust one another.

00:13:31.310 --> 00:13:34.730
You won't say who you are,
but shove cash in my face?

00:13:34.730 --> 00:13:38.650
You better have enough
to buy my trust, too.

00:13:38.650 --> 00:13:44.150
Could you please stop jabbering
and see if this is enough?

00:13:44.150 --> 00:13:45.780
Holy shit.

00:13:45.780 --> 00:13:48.030
Ain't you generous.

00:13:48.030 --> 00:13:53.500
As you just mentioned,
I've brought enough to buy your trust.

00:13:55.460 --> 00:13:59.670
Sure. I won't ask any questions
about who you work for.

00:13:59.670 --> 00:14:03.090
This here's payment enough.

00:14:03.090 --> 00:14:04.720
Here are the goods.

00:14:09.850 --> 00:14:12.810
Pleasure doing business with you.

00:14:16.270 --> 00:14:22.400
Shooting lessons are extra.
Does your boss know how to use that?

00:14:23.400 --> 00:14:24.990
Oh, yes.

00:14:25.070 --> 00:14:26.740
"Classroom"

00:14:26.990 --> 00:14:29.200
Huh? You wanna learn how to shoot a gun?

00:14:29.200 --> 00:14:32.410
Yes. I figured you might
have some knowledge.

00:14:32.410 --> 00:14:38.920
You figured right! This old fart learned
how to shoot from a foreign ex-soldier!

00:14:38.920 --> 00:14:40.960
As a member of our club,

00:14:40.960 --> 00:14:44.630
I thought it would be a fine idea to learn
how to use a variety of weapons!

00:14:44.630 --> 00:14:50.760
Sure. I've always wanted to do
a big watergun fight in club, too.

00:14:50.760 --> 00:14:52.050
I'll teach ya!

00:14:56.350 --> 00:14:57.390
What's that?

00:14:57.390 --> 00:14:59.310
Your training gun.

00:15:06.070 --> 00:15:10.110
Wow. This model gun is quite well-crafted.

00:15:10.110 --> 00:15:16.330
Right? It was specially made to have
the same weight as the real thing.

00:15:25.090 --> 00:15:26.920
I shouldn't be surprised!

00:15:26.920 --> 00:15:29.930
Remember what I just told you.

00:15:29.930 --> 00:15:34.390
The best way to get better
is lots and lots of practice.

00:15:34.390 --> 00:15:36.520
Practice makes perfect, as they say!

00:15:36.520 --> 00:15:40.140
My, I'm quite good at that.

00:16:31.860 --> 00:16:36.280
Not to worry. I'm quite accustomed
to handling firearms.

00:16:42.790 --> 00:16:43.960
Hello?

00:16:44.880 --> 00:16:48.050
Morning, Satoko-chan!
You sound like you just woke up!

00:16:48.050 --> 00:16:49.670
My, it's just you, Rena-san.

00:16:49.670 --> 00:16:52.260
What do you want so early in the morning?

00:16:52.260 --> 00:16:54.470
Good morning, Satoko!

00:16:54.470 --> 00:16:57.930
Mion-san is with you?
I know what that means.

00:16:57.930 --> 00:16:59.310
You sure do! Grab Rika-chan
and meet up in Okinomiya!

00:16:59.310 --> 00:17:03.100
"Saturday, June 11th"

00:16:59.310 --> 00:17:03.100
You sure do! Grab Rika-chan
and meet up in Okinomiya!

00:17:03.100 --> 00:17:05.730
"Sunday, June 12th"

00:17:03.100 --> 00:17:05.730
You're coming, right?

00:17:05.730 --> 00:17:10.780
Absolutely! I'm coming
to destroy you, just you wait!

00:17:14.860 --> 00:17:17.240
Today's gonna be big!

00:17:17.240 --> 00:17:20.950
I heard Mion-san produced
the money for a cash price!

00:17:20.950 --> 00:17:24.040
A big one, too! Fifty thousand yen!

00:17:24.040 --> 00:17:27.290
That's enough money
to make your head spin!

00:17:27.960 --> 00:17:28.790
"Da Vinci"

00:17:28.790 --> 00:17:30.420
"Da Vinci"

00:17:28.790 --> 00:17:30.420
My, there you are! We've been waiting!

00:17:30.420 --> 00:17:32.710
My, there you are! We've been waiting!

00:17:32.710 --> 00:17:34.840
Good morning, everyone.

00:17:34.840 --> 00:17:37.470
Hey! Morning, guys.

00:17:37.470 --> 00:17:40.760
Wait, is this where
we're having club today?!

00:17:40.760 --> 00:17:45.770
The shop holds game tournaments
every now and then to attract customers.

00:17:45.770 --> 00:17:50.690
That means all the guys in here
are gonna play in the tournament?

00:17:50.690 --> 00:17:56.910
That's right! Today, we get to play against
a lot more people than just ourselves!

00:17:56.910 --> 00:18:00.280
So I've gotta beat all of them, too...

00:18:00.280 --> 00:18:03.540
This is gonna be so much fun, Kei-chan.

00:18:11.250 --> 00:18:13.710
What?! You recovered from that already?!

00:18:15.380 --> 00:18:20.390
It's sooo kyute!
I wanna take them all home!

00:18:20.390 --> 00:18:25.930
I've never played the fishing game before.
Please go easy on me.

00:18:25.930 --> 00:18:30.310
Don't worry! We'll teach you how to play!

00:18:30.310 --> 00:18:38.320
All right, this old fart's gonna take you on.
Pick out a game you're good at.

00:18:38.320 --> 00:18:42.780
I've played you so many times,
I don't know how many this makes.

00:18:42.780 --> 00:18:46.830
Huh? But we just met today, didn't we?

00:18:48.540 --> 00:18:50.710
I've memorized them all.

00:18:59.380 --> 00:19:01.510
--Whoa, no way!
--Are you psychic or something?!

00:19:03.140 --> 00:19:04.720
Have a gander at this!

00:19:04.720 --> 00:19:06.810
Victory is mine!

00:19:07.770 --> 00:19:09.270
That was far too easy.

00:19:09.270 --> 00:19:12.690
H-Holy crap, you won already?!

00:19:12.690 --> 00:19:14.440
Nicely done, Satoko.

00:19:14.440 --> 00:19:16.820
I expected no less
of you, either, Mion-san.

00:19:16.820 --> 00:19:19.660
You're done too, Mion?! That fast?!

00:19:19.660 --> 00:19:26.040
Well then, Mion-san, shall we go have some
tea while we wait for the others to win?

00:19:26.040 --> 00:19:28.500
Hey, great idea!

00:19:34.880 --> 00:19:36.920
What should I get to drink?

00:19:36.920 --> 00:19:38.340
How about this!

00:19:48.680 --> 00:19:50.270
A thought, Eua-san.

00:19:50.270 --> 00:19:51.520
What is it?

00:19:51.520 --> 00:19:56.280
There were no worlds where
Mion-san lost herself to paranoia.

00:19:56.280 --> 00:19:58.070
That's correct.

00:19:58.070 --> 00:20:02.990
Hinamizawa Syndrome is triggered in those
who are physically distant from the Queen

00:20:02.990 --> 00:20:07.910
or those who are experiencing
increased mental stress.

00:20:07.910 --> 00:20:10.660
And while Mion-san seems emotional,

00:20:10.660 --> 00:20:14.330
she's actually quite
the logical thinker. Is that why?

00:20:14.330 --> 00:20:21.300
That, or her sense of duty as the next head
of the Sonozakis bolsters her resolve.

00:20:21.300 --> 00:20:22.720
In either case,

00:20:22.720 --> 00:20:28.680
I wonder what Mion-san would do
if she were to be afflicted?

00:20:28.680 --> 00:20:31.480
I must say, I'm curious.

00:20:33.850 --> 00:20:37.440
Sorry, guys. I'll make it up
to you next time, promise!

00:20:37.440 --> 00:20:41.030
We'll have to continue
the fun later, then!

00:20:41.030 --> 00:20:43.990
Thanks to you guys,
the shop made a huge profit today!

00:20:43.990 --> 00:20:45.950
Here's a little something to say thanks.

00:20:46.990 --> 00:20:50.410
Hey, Uncle Yoshiro,
where's my little something?

00:20:50.410 --> 00:20:53.920
I'll give you a big tip
next time I see you at work.

00:20:53.920 --> 00:20:54.960
No fair.

00:20:54.960 --> 00:20:57.750
--Oh, my!
--This is so cute!

00:20:57.750 --> 00:21:00.960
Can I really take this home?!

00:21:00.960 --> 00:21:02.840
Is mine cute, too...?

00:21:05.140 --> 00:21:06.930
It's sooo kyute!

00:21:08.140 --> 00:21:11.390
That's the last thing
I'd expect you to want, Kei-chan!

00:21:11.390 --> 00:21:13.140
I'll admit it's cute,

00:21:13.140 --> 00:21:15.350
but I can't say a doll
like this is for me...

00:21:15.350 --> 00:21:19.980
If you took that home,
everyone'd think you were a total perv.

00:21:19.980 --> 00:21:23.150
Yeah, it's really not my thing.

00:21:26.370 --> 00:21:27.820
Keiichi.

00:21:29.120 --> 00:21:31.200
As long as you're kind about it,

00:21:31.200 --> 00:21:36.120
you could give it to anyone, and they
wouldn't be flustered, they'd accept it!

00:21:38.460 --> 00:21:42.130
Here, Mion, you have it.
You'll get more use out of it than me.

00:21:42.130 --> 00:21:45.930
Huh?! But I'm so not the type for dolls!

00:21:45.930 --> 00:21:50.680
Like, I'm always wondering why I wasn't
just born a guy or something, you know?

